<p>Find the dimensionless (unitless) terms among the following concentration expressions.</p>
&nbsp;

<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="min-width: 300px;"><tbody><tr><td>(a)</td><td>Molality</td><td>(b)</td><td>Molarity</td></tr><tr><td>(c)</td><td>Mole fraction</td><td>(d)</td><td>Mass percent</td></tr></tbody></table>
Choose the correct option:

<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="min-width: 300px;"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td>(a), (b)</td><td>2.</td><td>(b), (c)</td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td>(a), (b), (c)</td><td>4.</td><td>(c), (d)</td></tr></tbody></table>

Given below are two statements:&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Assertion&nbsp;(A):</strong></td><td>1 a.m.u = 1 .66 &times; 10<sup>&minus;24</sup> gram.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Reason&nbsp;(R):</strong></td><td>The actual mass of one atom of C-12 is equal to&nbsp;1.99 &times; 10<sup>-23</sup> g.</td></tr></tbody></table>
&nbsp;

<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td>Both&nbsp;<strong>(A)</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;are True and&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;is the correct explanation of&nbsp;<strong>(A)</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td>2.</td><td>Both&nbsp;<strong>(A)</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;are True but&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;is not the correct explanation of&nbsp;<strong>(A)</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td><strong>(A)</strong>&nbsp;is True but&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;is False.</td></tr><tr><td>4.</td><td><strong>(A)</strong>&nbsp;is False but&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;is True.</td></tr></tbody></table>

The incorrect statements regarding 1 mole of dioxygen gas at STP among the four statements is/are:&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="min-width: 300px;"><tbody><tr><td>(a)</td><td>16 g of gas</td></tr><tr><td>(b)</td><td>22.9&nbsp;L of gas</td></tr><tr><td>(c)</td><td><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>022</mn><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>23</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;dioxygen molecules</td></tr><tr><td>(d)</td><td>11.2 L of gas</td></tr></tbody></table>
&nbsp;

